<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 22 May, from 337 to 1972.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantine-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">337 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,689 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Constantine the Great dies near Nicomedia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The first Christian Roman emperor died after being baptised on his deathbed. He had founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, and the empire was divided among his three sons.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">853 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,173 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Byzantine navy sacks Damietta in the Nile Delta</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Byzantine fleet sacked Damietta on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile-delta">Nile Delta</a> while its garrison was absent, taking captives and weapons intended for the Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>. The shocked Abbasid authorities refortified the coasts and strengthened the local fleet.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arab-byzantine-wars">Arab–Byzantine wars</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile-delta">Nile Delta</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1246">1246 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">780 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry Raspe is elected anti-king of Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With papal backing, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-raspe">Henry Raspe</a>, Landgrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>, was elected anti-king in opposition to Conrad IV, son of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a>. He defeated Conrad on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nidda">Nidda</a> in August but died the next year, leaving no heir.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-raspe">Henry Raspe</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1455">1455 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">571 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Yorkists win the First Battle of St Albans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Richard, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a>, defeated royal forces in the streets of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-albans">St Albans</a> and took Henry VI into his custody. The clash is usually seen as the opening battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-roses">Wars of the Roses</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1762">1762 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">264 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Hamburg takes Sweden out of the Seven Years' War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> made peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, restoring the pre-war borders. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s withdrawal that same month, the treaty relieved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great">Frederick the Great</a> of two enemies.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-sweden">Kingdom of Sweden</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1856">1856 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">170 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Senator Charles Sumner is beaten on the floor of the Senate</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Congressman Preston Brooks attacked the anti-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> senator with a cane after Sumner's speech against slavery in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kansas">Kansas</a>. The assault deepened the bitterness between North and South.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1906">1906 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">120 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wright brothers receive their patent for a flying machine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The US Patent Office granted Orville and Wilbur Wright patent 821,393 for their method of controlling an aircraft. They spent years defending it in the courts.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1972">1972 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">54 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ceylon becomes the Republic of Sri Lanka</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A new constitution made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a> a republic, ending the British monarch's role as head of state, and adopted the name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>. The island had become independent in 1948.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 22 May <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-de-buade-de-frontenac"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-de-buade-de-frontenac.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis de Buade de Frontenac</span><span class="tp">1622–1698</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ram-mohan-roy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ram-mohan-roy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ram Mohan Roy</span><span class="tp">1772–1833</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/arthur-conan-doyle"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/arthur-conan-doyle.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Arthur Conan Doyle</span><span class="tp">1859–1930</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/d-f-malan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/d-f-malan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">D. F. Malan</span><span class="tp">1874–1959</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/symon-petliura"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/symon-petliura.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Symon Petliura</span><span class="tp">1879–1926</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/giacomo-matteotti"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/giacomo-matteotti.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Giacomo Matteotti</span><span class="tp">1885–1924</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/herge"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/herge.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hergé</span><span class="tp">1907–1983</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 22 May <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francesco-guicciardini"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francesco-guicciardini.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francesco Guicciardini</span><span class="tp">1483–1540</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sher-shah-suri"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sher-shah-suri.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sher Shah Suri</span><span class="tp">c. 1486–1545</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-of-the-two-sicilies"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-ii-of-the-two-sicilies.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ferdinand II of the Two Sicilies</span><span class="tp">1810–1859</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/victor-hugo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/victor-hugo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Victor Hugo</span><span class="tp">1802–1885</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ernst-toller"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ernst-toller.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ernst Toller</span><span class="tp">1893–1939</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
